      "content": "When you mention \"human-induced friction,\" do you mean it's more about the mental load on the drivers at the entry points? I'm specifically interested in why these interruptions seem so disruptive to the flow—sometimes it feels like a single car's hesitation causes a disproportionate amount of chaos that seems almost... unpredictable or chaotic beyond just standard human error. Is there a specific way to classify that kind of disruption in modeling?",
